found by `zcat`-ing the contents of `/usr/share/man`!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894344626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894477732","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310#issuecomment-894477732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310","id":894477732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE841UKWk","user":{"login":"alejandro-colomar","id":21089465,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDg5NDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21089465?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar","html_url":"https://github.com/alejandro-colomar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-06T19:36:35Z","updated_at":"2021-08-06T19:36:35Z","body":"> @alejandro-colomar, welcome to SPDX!\r\n\r\n:-)\r\n\r\n> \r\n> We'd need some more information about the license to see if it fulfils the [License Inclusion Principles](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/master/DOCS/license-inclusion-principles.md) for the SPDX License List. Please could you include in this GitHub issue the same information that is asked for in our [online tools form](https://tools.spdx.org/app/submit_new_license/)? That would be very much appreciated; thanks! :)\r\n\r\nLicense's full name: `Verbatim`\r\nShort identifier: `Verbatim`\r\nSource / URL: <https://www.kernel.org/doc/man-pages/licenses.html>\r\nOSI status: I don't know; probably not submitted.  DFSG-compatible (no doubt man-pages ships with Debian), although not listed on Debian's website either.\r\nStandard license header:  None; the full text of the license is used.\r\nLicense text:\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n.\\\" Copyright (c) <year>, <copyright holder>\r\n.\\\" \r\n.\\\" %%%LICENSE_START(VERBATIM)\r\n.\\\" Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies of this\r\n.\\\" manual provided the copyright notice and this permission notice are\r\n.\\\" preserved on all copies.\r\n.\\\"\r\n.\\\" Permission is granted to copy and distribute modified versions of\r\n.\\\" this manual under the conditions for verbatim copying, provided that\r\n.\\\" the entire resulting derived work is distributed under the terms of\r\n.\\\" a permission notice identical to this one.\r\n.\\\"\r\n.\\\" Since the Linux kernel and libraries are constantly changing, this\r\n.\\\" manual page may be incorrect or out-of-date.  The author(s) assume.\r\n.\\\" no responsibility for errors or omissions, or for damages resulting.\r\n.\\\" from the use of the information contained herein.  The author(s) may.\r\n.\\\" not have taken the same level of care in the production of this.\r\n.\\\" manual, which is licensed free of charge, as they might when working.\r\n.\\\" professionally.\r\n.\\\"\r\n.\\\" Formatted or processed versions of this manual, if unaccompanied by\r\n.\\\" the source, must acknowledge the copyright and authors of this work.\r\n.\\\" %%%LICENSE_END\r\n```\r\n\r\nWho is the license author or license steward?  I don't know.  Probably some previous maintainer of the man-pages.  Michael Kerrisk <mtk.manpages@gmail.com> probably has more information about this.\r\n\r\nExample project URL: <https://www.kernel.org/doc/man-pages/>\r\n\r\n> \r\n> You can, in this case, omit the 'example project URLs' field - this request is unusual in that such examples of use can be readily found by `zcat`-ing the contents of `/usr/share/man`!\r\n\r\n:-}  Anyway, I added it for completeness.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894477732/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894850697","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310#issuecomment-894850697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310","id":894850697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE841VlaJ","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-08T20:23:53Z","updated_at":"2021-08-08T20:23:53Z","body":"Doing a quick inclusion-principles review on this one:\r\n\r\n**Definitive factors**: meets all of these. Looks like the first two sentences are very close to [Abstyles](https://spdx.org/licenses/Abstyles.html) and part of [Latex2e](https://spdx.org/licenses/Latex2e), but the remainder of the license is different so this can't really use either of those IDs.\r\n\r\n**Other factors**:\r\n\r\n1. Yes, I'd say this meets the Free Cultural Works definition. Permits redistribution, modifying, etc., with a strong copyleft/sharealike-style requirement for modified versions.\r\n2. Yes, generally usable by anyone\r\n3. Actual, substantial use: very yes, it seems  :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n4. N/A, since meets Free Cultural Works definition.\r\n5. Not clear re: steward, but for short permission notices like this I think there frequently might not be a \"license steward\" the same way there is for more formal, titled licenses.\r\n\r\nGiven all of that, I'm a +1 to add this to the License List.\r\n\r\n= = = = =\r\n\r\nTwo specific comments about _how_ it gets added:\r\n1. For the license ID, I might be inclined to go with something like `Verbatim-man-pages` instead of just `Verbatim` -- since this one seems pretty specific to manual pages (and refers to them in the license text). I don't feel super-strongly about this, but I think it might be a good idea here.\r\n2. For the actual license text that gets added to the list: from a pedantic SPDX view, I'm noticing those extra periods at the end-of-line for the third paragraph -- see below, stripping the prefix characters, but leaving those in place:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSince the Linux kernel and libraries are constantly changing, this\r\nmanual page may be incorrect or out-of-date.  The author(s) assume.\r\nno responsibility for errors or omissions, or for damages resulting.\r\nfrom the use of the information contained herein.  The author(s) may.\r\nnot have taken the same level of care in the production of this.\r\nmanual, which is licensed free of charge, as they might when working.\r\nprofessionally.\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo me it looks like those stray periods might have been inadvertent (since they don't show up in the other paragraphs).\r\n\r\nAssuming this is approved to add to the License List, I might suggest leaving those stray periods in the XML, but tagging them as `<optional></optional>`. That way, license checkers that are pedantic about punctuation will handle them correctly, and those that aren't will disregard them anyway.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894850697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894851594","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310#issuecomment-894851594","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310","id":894851594,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE841VloK","user":{"login":"alejandro-colomar","id":21089465,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDg5NDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21089465?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar","html_url":"https://github.com/alejandro-colomar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alejandro-colomar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-08T20:32:36Z","updated_at":"2021-08-08T20:33:02Z","body":"Re: Verbatim-man-pages: yes, thay identifier seems reasonable to me.\r\n\r\nRe: nonsensical periods: I think that's a typo in the license example text in the website, and they are not present in the license texts in the actual manual pages, so you can safely remove them.\r\n\r\nIf you need me to resend the text, as present in actual pages (without the periods) I can do that","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894851594/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/894863542","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310#issuecomment-894863542","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1310","id":894863542,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE841Voi2","user":{"login":"seabass-labrax","id":79224200,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MjI0MjAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79224200?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax","html_url":"https://github.com/seabass-labrax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sea